From: (fill in)
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/gpu: prefault dma-buf blob mappings

A blob resource exported as a dma-buf is mapped into the virtio-gpu shm
region with mmap(MAP_FIXED). The resulting VMA is VM_PFNMAP: it carries no
struct page and is not managed like ordinary memory.

    fff854810000-fff854814000 rw-s 105cc8000 00:0c 99   /dmabuf:
    VmFlags: rd wr sh mr mw ms pf de dd
                              ^^ VM_PFNMAP

KVM cannot fault such memory in on its own. When the guest writes to a page
of the mapping that has no writable PTE yet, the fault is resolved through
hva_to_pfn_remapped(), which finds no writable PTE and returns
KVM_PFN_ERR_RO_FAULT; user_mem_abort() then fails with -EFAULT and KVM_RUN
tears the VM down:

    ERROR krun_vmm::linux::vstate] Failure during vcpu run: Bad address (os error 14)

On Apple Silicon under muvm this makes every GPU-accelerated workload die the
moment the guest touches the GPU. Blobs backed by a memfd are unaffected;
their VMAs have ordinary flags.

Establishing the PTEs is up to the VMM, so walk the fresh mapping once and
rewrite every page with the value it already holds. Contents are unchanged,
but a writable PTE exists before the guest ever reaches the page.

Applied only to DMABUF exports, so memfd-backed blobs keep their lazy
faulting, and only to read-write mappings, where the read-modify-write is
safe and where the write path in KVM is reachable at all.

MAP_POPULATE would not do: populate_vma_page_range() goes through
__get_user_pages(), which rejects VM_PFNMAP VMAs in check_vma_flags(), and
mm_populate() discards the error.

The cost is that every page of a dma-buf blob is faulted in at map time
instead of on demand.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: opus-5

